course: dictionary
lesson: 7901
title: Rarity and value
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A rarity is a thing that is rare, which means it is not often seen or found. Rarity is also the quality of being rare. The ending -ity turns the word rare into a noun, so rarity names that quality.
explain: Rarity helps explain why some things are worth a lot. «Very high art prices come from fame, history, rarity and buyers competing at auctions.» The sentence lists rarity with fame and history, so rarity is one reason a picture can be so valuable.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Prices come from how rare something is" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Always read the words around a new word to find its clues.
fact: Rarity means how rare something is, or the quality of being rare.
fact: A rarity is a thing that is rare, so it is not often seen or found.
fact: In trading card games, rarity levels such as common, rare and legendary show how hard a card is to find.
fact: «A real rarity» means something very unusual that you seldom see.
fact: Rarity often makes an item more valuable, as in «because of its rarity».
exercise: «Very high art prices come from fame, history, rarity and buyers competing at auctions.» In this sentence, what does rarity mean? | How old a picture is | How many people visit a gallery | *How rare something is, so it is not often found | How loudly something is played
exercise: In trading card games, what do rarity levels like common, rare and legendary show? | *How hard a card is to find | The colour of the card's back | How big the card is | The name of the game
exercise: Which word fits best? «The stamp is worth a lot because of its ___.» | weather | *rarity | breakfast | noise
test: A rarity is a thing that is rare. What does rare mean? | Very wet | Very loud | *Not often seen or found | Seen every day in every town
test: Which word fits best? «Scientists were thrilled, because the orchid was a real ___.» | sandwich | rainbow | *rarity | whisper
exam: «Because of its rarity, the painting sold for millions.» Why did the painting sell for so much? | It makes a loud noise | It is very large | It was painted in a single afternoon | *It is not often found, so buyers want it very badly
